  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 602.33 Mean high water",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 602.33 “Mean high water” means the average of all the high water heights observed over the National Tidal Datum Epoch (NTDE), or over an equivalent datum derived for stations with shorter series by comparison of simultaneous observation with a control tide station.\n\nSource. #12806, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt600.html"
